# Copy this file to ".env" (same folder as package.json) and fill in your values.
# Both values are required. Without them the app shows a "Connect to Supabase" setup screen.
#
# Find both values in Supabase: Project Settings -> API
#   VITE_SUPABASE_URL      = Project URL, e.g. https://abcdxyz.supabase.co
#   VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY = the LEGACY "anon" key (starts with eyJ...). Use this one, not sb_publishable_...:
#                            the AI Edge Function checks a JWT, which sb_publishable keys are not.
#                            (Project Settings -> API Keys -> "Legacy anon, service_role API keys" tab)
#
# NEVER put the service_role / secret key here. Anything starting with VITE_
# is bundled into the browser code and visible to everyone.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# The Gemini API key is NOT put here. It is a Supabase secret (see README, "Deploy the AI function").
